{"title":"1992 AHSME Problems/Problem 19","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AHSME_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For each vertex of a solid cube, consider the tetrahedron determined by the vertex and the midpoints of the three edges that meet at that vertex. The portion of the cube that remains when these eight tetrahedra are cut away is called a cubeoctahedron. The ratio of the volume of the cubeoctahedron to the volume of the original cube is closest to which of these?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a173d5212a325478aa5d24cda35e9dde8c3f4c72.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A) } 75\\%\\quad \\text{(B) } 78\\%\\quad \\text{(C) } 81\\%\\quad \\text{(D) } 84\\%\\quad \\text{(E) } 87\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"387\" height=\"19\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AHSME_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/8/25809e4f87f20a2ee949878bc603b9eda09422ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\fbox{D}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"26\" height=\"24\" /> Let the cube have side length 1, and place the cube in the coordinate plane. Then we can pick any vertex, get the coordinates of the midpoints, and hence find the three vectors that define the tetrahedron (the vectors from the chosen vertex to each midpoint). Now using <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/5/ba5ff7a26ca6393d225d9138dff47ea096598c64.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{6}\\|a.(b\\times c)\\|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"100\" height=\"38\" />, we can find the volume of one of the tetrahedra, then multiply it by 8, and subtract from 1 to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/3/5533bc48602603f16d18c04858cad119c04833c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{5}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />, which is closest to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/c/6fceca304ecdebbd0bcdbf2c1c7a312dd8a24465.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$84\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"35\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AHSME_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AHSME\" title=\"1992 AHSME\">1992 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1992 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1992 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1992\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AHSME_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"1992 AHSME Problems/Problem 18\">Problem 18</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AHSME_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"1992 AHSME Problems/Problem 20\">Problem 20</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1992 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1992 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1992 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1992 AHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1992 AHSME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1992 AHSME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AHSME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1992 AHSME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AHSME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1992 AHSME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AHSME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1992 AHSME Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AHSME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1992 AHSME Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AHSME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1992 AHSME Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AHSME_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"1992 AHSME Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AHSME_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"1992 AHSME Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AHSME_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"1992 AHSME Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AHSME_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"1992 AHSME Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AHSME_Pro